📖 Step-by-Step Instructions After Unzipping

Follow these 4 steps to activate your zero-dependency, multi-persona engine in your project workspace:

Step 1: Extract into Your Project Root

Unzip the contents directly into your main project directory (e.g., alongside your frontend/backend code folders). Ensure the .ai-agency/ hidden folder sits at the root level:
text
your-project-root/
├── .ai-agency/                  # Holds the 8 core persona rules
├── .github/workflows/           # Pre-configured CI/CD workflow
├── bin/                         # Local execution scripts
├── AGENTS.md                    # Core persona catalog layout
├── README.md                    # Quick-start documentation handbook
├── setup-git-alias.sh           # Global terminal shortcut setup script
├── jest.config.js               # Frontend 85% coverage guardrail
└── pytest.ini                   # Backend 85% coverage guardrail
Use code with caution.

Step 2: Provision Your Global Terminal Shortcut

Open your standard operating system terminal, navigate to your project directory, and run the alias provisioning script:
bash
chmod +x setup-git-alias.sh && ./setup-git-alias.sh

This binds your local shell script to your global Git runtime engine, allowing you to trigger code checks anywhere using git agency-review.

Step 3: Driving the Pipeline in Your AI Assistant Chat Panel

Because this setup is entirely file-based and IDE-agnostic, you guide the AI team by referencing your local markdown files directly inside Cursor, Windsurf, or VS Code + Copilot:
• For Phase 1 (Planning):"I want to add an email magic-link log-in flow. @1_business_analyst.md run /brief to initialize the project targets, then @2_product_manager.md run /shard to build our atomic story markdown documents."
• For Phase 2 (Development):"@1_scrum_master.md isolate story_01. Then @2_developer.md use command /build to write code satisfying only that specific story file."

Step 4: Run a Automated Phase 3 Code Review Loop

Whenever you have changed files (whether they are staged or unstaged in Git), open your regular terminal and run:
bash
git agency-review
Use code with caution.
1. The script will sweep your modified lines (git diff) and auto-generate a master diagnostic index file inside docs/planning/active_review_diff.md.
2. It will output a terminal macro snippet. Paste that snippet into your AI chat window:@.ai-agency/agency.md @docs/planning/active_review_diff.md /review
3. The AI assistant will parse the diff across all 8 personas, calculate individual approvals, and cleanly generate a permanent, timestamped Markdown Review Report with your mandatory sign-off format inside your docs/reviews/ directory.
